    "created_at": "2017-10-09T09:01:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-09T09:01:28Z",
    "body": "> The proposal is to introduce a new special element named `<shadowroot>` that if found in an HTML input stream ends up creating a shadow tree associated with its immediate parent. Any elements inside it end up in that shadow tree. It can be nested.\r\n\r\nThat sounds a lot like `<template>`. How exactly would this be different?\r\n\r\n(Please assume that I don't know how shadow trees work.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/335100937/reactions",
