    "body": "@hsivonen mainly in that `<shadowroot>` itself does not end up in the tree. It's a declarative form of `parentElement.attachShadow()` (see https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-element-attachshadow). Also, the elements (and the `ShadowRoot` object) would not have a different node document from _parentElement_, meaning scripts would still execute, images would load, etc.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
