    "created_at": "2017-10-09T11:03:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-09T11:03:32Z",
    "body": "I think the use cases would have to be overwhelmingly strong for this to be a good idea. `<template>` changing some invariants resulting in one or two security bugs in Gecko. `<isindex>` turned out to be quite an annoyance right before its removal after being inert sunk cost for years.\r\n\r\nAre the use cases overwhelmingly strong? Do we even have enough experience with Shadow DOM to know if this would be nice in theory or something that Web developers are really missing?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
