    "created_at": "2017-10-10T22:33:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-10T22:33:00Z",
    "body": "Note: My *original* proposal is just \"have a way to do declarative shadow DOM, because requiring JS for this is bad in many ways\". Please read <https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/510> for details - I listed a whole bunch of reasons why this feels like a worthwhile addition to the platform (and why current solutions are unsatisfactory).\r\n\r\nIn particular, I did not have any preferred syntax for this. My original *suggested* syntax was `template` with some attributes indicating that it should auto-add its contents to its parent as a shadow tree upon being inserted into the tree.  (Afterwards, it would just be an ordinary dead `template`; behavior upon removing/re-adding the element left undecided.)  Anne and some others believed this would be better (better perf, less confusing behavior with leftover \"dead\" elements) if this was a parser macro instead.\r\n\r\nPlease do not let dissatisfaction with any particular syntax approach dissuade you from the idea in general. As argued in the DOM thread, I think there's strong use-cases for this functionality.\r\n\r\n(Separately, @rniwa wants to wait on this and make sure it's compatible with a fuller proposal for declarative custom elements, so we don't duplicate work or have minor syntax/functionality incongruities. They're planning to present this proposal at TPAC, I believe.)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
