    "created_at": "2017-10-10T23:31:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-10T23:31:26Z",
    "body": "I think @hsivonen was making a statement about the particular proposal to add `shadowroot` as a parser macro, and I agree with him that such a parser macro has a significant implementation cost and should be supported by very strong use cases. I don't believe the use cases listed thus far are strong enough to justify this. Thus, our current consensus at Apple is that `shadowroot` element as currently proposed is a non-starter.\r\n\r\nHaving said that, I'm supportive of adding a mechanism to attach a shadow tree on an element without JS, in particular using `template` element, and we're discussing the design for it internally at Apple to be submitted prior to TPAC.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
